      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is OPFS and why is it required for SQLite in the browser?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Origin Private File System (OPFS) is a high-performance, private filesystem endpoint exposed via the File System Access API. Unlike localStorage or IndexedDB, OPFS provides synchronous in-place byte-range read/write operations inside dedicated Web Workers (via FileSystemSyncAccessHandle), enabling full SQLite ACID transactions and write-ahead logging (WAL) at near-native SSD speeds."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does client-side AES-GCM encryption protect SQLite data?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
